    "body": "@jakearchibald  1) Anytime; 2) Any format which can be immediately played at a media element without the other portion of the original resource; for example if the original file is `.mp4`, though need to be converted to `.ogg` to get 5 seconds of media as a discrete file, that is ok; 3) Any number of uses for media - a) play the media fragemnt immediately; b) send the media fragment as `Blob` or `ArrayBuffer` to another user or service; c) concatenate the media fragment with another, unrelated media fragment to create a mix of media.\r\n\r\nThe primary issue is range request returns expected result for range `bytes=0-1024*1024`, though not `bytes=1024*1024-1024*1024*32`. And with current workaround more than 30 generated `Blob`s crash tab of browser.\r\n\r\nThe actual problem is: How to request and get any segment of a media resource as a distinct and discrete resource, capable of being played back without reliance on the other portion of the media resource.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
